WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.035
-Our first guest tonight is
an Emmy Award-winning actor,

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.538
director, and producer you know
from his work in iconic films

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.807
such as "One Flew Over
the Cuckoo's Nest," "Twins," and

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.743
"Matilda," and shows like "It's
Always Sunny in Philadelphia."

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.145
He stars in the animated series,
"Little Demon,"

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:15.447
which airs Thursday nights
on FXX.

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:17.884
It is available to stream on
Hulu the next day.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.018
Let's take a look.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.154
-This is the metaphysical realm.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.688
-Hmm, fancy.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.723
-Hipsters call it the fringe,

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:27.059
which makes me want to punch
a hole in my face.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:30.296
It's like the central hub
for all unearthly realms.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.434
Think port authority but with
much, much, much more urine

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.069
and fewer bomb threats.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.937
-So, if I call the shots,
does that mean

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.238
I don't have to listen
to anyone?

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.406
-Look at that guy.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.575
He's got a bird head
and he craps bubbles.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.577
I thought that was pretty cool.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.045
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.915
the legendary Danny DeVito,
everybody!

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.983
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:58.157 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:05.364 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:12.539 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.840
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.742
So happy you're here!

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.778
-Great to be here, buddy boy.
-How have you been?

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.213
-Really well. Really well.
Thank you.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.148
-This is very exciting.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.317
You're playing the devil.
-Yes, very close to home, yeah.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.752
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.420
-I don't know if people can
quite tell from the clip

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.488
'cause, you know, you would hear
your voice, but that does not --

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:30.523
you do not look in the clip
like the devil.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.191
-Let me do the devil thing.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.760
-I'm doing the devil thing
in real life.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.229
-Yeah.
-Easy. [ Grunts ]

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.964
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:42.034
-Yeah, no, so I -- we --
"Little Demon" is a comedy.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.802
It's not for kiddies.

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:47.307
It's on FXX at 10:00
on Thursday nights.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.542
And then it goes to Hulu,
like you said.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.311
And, you know, it's just been
a blast because I'm working with

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:55.815
my daughter Lucy,
and my son, Jake.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.618
And it's just off the charts
wonderful.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.220
-So, Lucy is actually
the voice of --

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.056
-Of Chrissy, who is
the little demon.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.758
She's the offspring
of the devil.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.892
-Yeah.
-So, yeah.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:09.295
She's the devil's spawn,
as you would.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.297
And Aubrey Plaza
plays her mommy.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.666
-Right.
-Aubrey is just -- Yeah.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.102
-A very believable mother
of a demon.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.304
-She's tough. She's a tough --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.806
She's a tough cookie,
let's put it that way.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.808
-She is, a tough
and talented cookie.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.643
One of our favorites.
-A very talented cookie.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.979
And so, you know, the idea is
that she's been --

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:31.718
She had the baby, and she knows
it's the devil's -- mine.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.653
And she's been hiding it from me
for 13 years.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:36.055
And then what happens?

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:39.926
You know, usually when you're
13-ish and you're a woman,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.927
you know what happens?
-Mm-hmm?

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.696
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.664
-I mean, I think
if you don't know, it's --

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:47.566
you're the person to tell.
-That's right.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.303
[ Laughter ]
So anyway.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:53.606
At that stage in her life
when she has her period --

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.640
-Yep.
-I'll say it.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.208
-Yeah, great.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.208 --> 00:03:02.982
-She also starts realizing
these powers that she has.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:06.452
And then she finds out
that her dad is not --

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:11.157
her mom told her that her dad
was not alive.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.060
So, she finds out her dad
is the devil.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:18.130
And that's me. And I come back
to insinuate myself in her life.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.598
-[ Laughs ]
That is a wonderful premise.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.301
-Yeah.
-And Lucy brought it to you?

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.936
-Yes, absolutely.
She called me one day, she said,

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.573
"Dad, we're thinking about doing
'Little Demon.'

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.409
There's a part
you were born to play."

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.077
I said, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:34.180
She said, "Satan."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.382
Well, yeah.
It's a multifaceted part.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.318
There's a lot to deal with when
you're the prince of darkness.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.753
-Yeah, absolutely.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.490
-Nobody ever talks about just
the logistics of the day-to-day.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.059
-You got to deal with people
who want your job.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.561
-Right.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.496
-Tony Soprano thought
he had it bad.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.365
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah. But
the devil, on the other hand.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:57.203
But this is not the first time,
even in recent history,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.604
that you and Lucy
have worked together.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.072
You guys were just doing a play
up in Vermont together?

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.608
-That's right.
We went to Vermont to --

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.643
Theresa Rebeck wrote us a play.

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:07.113
We have a three-hander,
like, three-character play.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.548
And we workshopped it
at Dorset, Vermont.

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:10.983
It was great.
We had a great time.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.117
Four days up there.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:13.886
-Had you ever been on stage
with her before?

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.788
-We've done things -- No.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:20.893
Well -- No, we've never done,
like, a theater piece together.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.128
She's done a lot of theater.
I've done a lot of theater.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:24.830
We've always wanted to work
together.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:30.069
And now, we also are going to go
on stage to do a play,

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.871
which is like --
-So, I have to ask as a father.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.539
Because, obviously as an actor,
you're on stage,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.643
and you have to forget who you
are and become the character.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:40.046
But as a dad, I can't imagine
being on stage

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:44.217
and not being proud of your --
-Oh. Oh, God. Off the charts.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.818
-Does it get in the way
of being an actor?

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.521
-No, no, no. You've got to --
like, off the charts proud.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.357
I mean, just, like, the fact
that she's in there doing it.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.159
She and Jake are producing it.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.628
It's like, you know, it's --
it's big-time stuff.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:58.498
And animation is, like,
so complex and everything.

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.466
And I'm very, very proud of her.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:06.272
In the show, I'm desperate to
be -- to spend time with her.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:09.042
See? That's the whole idea,
the deadbeat dad --

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.143
I'm not a deadbeat dad,
I'm just saying.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.578
You know, I'm like --
I'm the guy

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.081
who she's been hiding
the kid from.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:18.217
So I'm desperate to spend time
with her.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.652
I'm working my way out.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.421
So, it's like a -- There's
a little family drama in there.

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:26.459
You know, when you're separated
parents and you're trying to vie

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:30.228
for the attention of
your precious daughter.

00:05:30.228 --> 00:05:34.100
In my case, you know,
I get her every other weekend.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.568
Which is not bad.
-Yeah.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.136
-But I'd like her every week.
-Yeah.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.704
-I'd like to show her things.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.639
-I want to show her the --
-Yeah.

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.275
Even the devil
wants to be a good dad.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.609
-I want to be a good dad.
-Yeah, that's good.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.077
-And I want to teach her things.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:48.247
And I want to be a good role
model for my kid.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:51.884
-Obviously in real life,
you have been a good role model.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.219
All three of your kids
are in show business.

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:55.688
-Yes.
-Are you surprised by that?

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:58.658
-Well, no, I'm not surprised
because they, you know, were,

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.693
like, born in a trunk
kind of thing.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.527
They were always on the stage.

00:06:02.527 --> 00:06:05.831
They were on the set all
the time with me and Rhea, and,

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:10.069
you know, always exposed to it
and the whole Hollywood thing.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.971
And they've turned out
really well.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:16.576
My middle kid, Gracie,
who is my middle daughter,

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.944
she's a painter.
-Oh, was she? She's an artist.

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:20.613
-Yes, she's in the arts.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:23.749
But Lucy's an actress
and Jake is doing the producing.

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:27.453
-What was the -- When they were
growing up, was there a piece of

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.522
yours that they were first drawn
to, seeing you on screen

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.759
that they liked?
-I think one of the scariest

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:36.128
things for me when is I did --
for me, was -- and for them,

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:37.997
I'm sure,
was when they watched me

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.699
get into makeup for the Penguin.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.733
-Yeah, 'cause that was really --
-That was brutal.

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:43.402
-That was pretty grotesque
makeup. Yeah.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:44.937
-That was really harsh.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.306
You know, and I have a picture
of the three of them, like,

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.909
staring around, looking at me
getting the --

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.577
you know, the things put on.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:54.446
But, you know, they were always,
like, really cool about it,

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:56.382
you know, being around
all the showbiz types.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.551
-Well, that's great.
And I do think it's a tribute

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.486
to you and Rhea that they wanted
to choose that life.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:03.188
-They wanted to do it, yeah.
-I got a lot more to ask you.

00:07:03.188 --> 00:07:04.957
We're going to be
right back with more

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:06.692
from Danny DeVito
right after this.

